<!--
  SK2023_Atm_datafit_binned_extra_dials.xml

  SUPPLEMENTARY dial-value source (Track S / Phase E2) for the binned-engine
  dials NOT in the production 131-dial value XML
  (SK2023_Atm_datafit_r2_fude_ccqe_full.xml) but resolved by some named spec.
  Two families:
    (a) base-name detector/flux stems (fcpc_separation, pc_reduction, etc.):
        the production XML carries only their ERA-SPLIT copies
        (stem_sk1 .. stem_sk45); the base-name form is used by the non-era
        specs (barr / updown / both / octsyst_*). nominal 1.0, sigma from the
        engine base SIGMA / DET_ERA value.
    (b) optional / diagnostic dials outside the production set (barr_zenith,
        decay_e_tagging, dir_smear, nmig_*, ntag_subgev_lowp / _highp,
        xsec_1p1h/2p2h/ccqe_subgev_nue): variant-spec dials.

  VALUES are transcribed verbatim from the engine dial tables (CANONICAL_DIALS),
  i.e. the E2 authority handoff, not invented. The engine loads this file
  ALONGSIDE the full-131 XML; together they cover every dial across all 26 named
  specs, so CANONICAL_DIALS is a pure hard-fail shadow. box children record the
  fit-time truncation limits (documentation; box authority stays in the
  fit_point dicts until a later phase). This file NEVER redeclares a
  production-131 dial (asserted at load: zero name overlap with the full XML).
-->
